From 404c6389b8fd933841ec1b1e9b8937318e8b2113 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 19:50:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sdm660: Describe the CPU CPRh, OSM and L2
 SAWs

Describe the CPU voltage and frequency hardware of SDM660, disabled by
default:

- The CPR fuse cells of both clusters in the QFPROM (speed bin, CPR
  fusing revision, and per fuse corner open-loop voltage, target
  quotient, ring oscillator and quotient offset), at the locations of
  the vendor CPRh driver.
- The silver and gold L2 SAWs.
- The two CPRh controllers (silver at 0x179c8000, gold at 0x179c4000) as
  one CPR3 power domain provider, with the RBCPR clock at 19.2 MHz. It
  keeps VDD_MX (active only) at nominal or above while it is bound, as
  the memory arrays run from MX below the APM threshold.
- The OSM frequency domains, sequencer regions and OSM clock RCG, with
  the GPLL0 based alternate clock and the L2 SAWs it waits for.

Also add the CPUs as cooling devices of the passive trips of the CPU
thermal zones: the four gold CPU sensors throttle the gold cluster and
the power cluster sensor throttles the silver cluster.

Board files add the corner plan (OPP tables) and enable the nodes.

Scope: SDM630/660 common
Porting notes: Local device tree addition (not upstream). Fuse locations from the vendor crDroid 4.19 drivers/regulator/cprh-kbss-regulator.c, register blocks from the vendor sdm660.dtsi, sdm660-regulator.dtsi and sdm660-pm.dtsi.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
